{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1366559-inhuman-senses","id":1366559,"title":"Inhuman Senses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-09T08:35:27-08:00","id":1366559,"title":"Inhuman Senses","content":"So rather a strange thing to me is that in both 2.5e and 3e there was never a formal definition given for inhuman senses. Not much of a problem except for how they relate to Excellencies.<br /> So my question is do Excellencies count as giving inhuman senses for the purpose of Charms that care about them? Additionally, what defines inhuman senses? Is it successes being given or does it have to be a physical trait of some kind or could just having superhumanly good senses count?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T08:42:11-08:00","id":1366561,"title":"","content":"Not sure what you call inhuman. However, for the purpose of powers that &quot;can only be contested by magic&quot;, Excellencies do count. I believe someone will surely give you a quote from the Ask the devs thread","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T09:15:31-08:00","id":1366571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1366559-inhuman-senses#post1366559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So rather a strange thing to me is that in both 2.5e and 3e there was never a formal definition given for inhuman senses. Not much of a problem except for how they relate to Excellencies.<br /> So my question is do Excellencies count as giving inhuman senses for the purpose of Charms that care about them? Additionally, what defines inhuman senses? Is it successes being given or does it have to be a physical trait of some kind or could just having superhumanly good senses count?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1207985#post1207985\">Excellencies is fine.</a><br /> <br /> I'd say the Merits that grant enhanced senses would be fine too.<br /> <br /> But you need <i>something</i> beyond normal senses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T09:36:30-08:00","id":1366576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1366559-inhuman-senses?p=1366571#post1366571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1207985#post1207985\">Excellencies is fine.</a><br /> <br /> I'd say the Merits that grant enhanced senses would be fine too.<br /> <br /> But you need <i>something</i> beyond normal senses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get this but if I'm a mortal that has say Perception 3, Awareness 3, I'd have more dice to roll than an Solar with Perception 1, Awareness 1 but doubling his pool with an Excellency, yet the Solar could see through things because he's using a Charm but mechanically and physically do nothing different?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This disguise cannot be pierced by mundane senses. Nor can it be thwarted by inhuman sensory acuity, such as the nose of a hound or the eye of a hawk. Senses heightened<br /> to supernatural levels by Charms such as Keen Sight Discipline have a chance to pierce this deception, but subtract 2 successes from their attempts </div> </div> </div>The way this is worded implies that charms have to be in the same vein as Keen Sight Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T09:41:46-08:00","id":1366578,"title":"","content":"For that specific instance, you'd need something like Keen Sight, not just an Excellency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T10:32:09-08:00","id":1366588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1366559-inhuman-senses?p=1366576#post1366576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get this but if I'm a mortal that has say Perception 3, Awareness 3, I'd have more dice to roll than an Solar with Perception 1, Awareness 1 but doubling his pool with an Excellency, yet the Solar could see through things because he's using a Charm but mechanically and physically do nothing different?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Because the Charm is magic.<br /> <br /> The difference is, literally, that the Solar is using magic and the mortal isn't.<br /> <br /> A mortal might be a champion high jumper with 5 dots of Athletics, but they can't jump to the top of a twenty foot wall in a single bound because this is impossible. A Solar with Athletics 2 and Monkey Leap Technique CAN jump to the top of that wall... by using magic.<br /> <br /> Charms, including Excellencies, do not exist (see page 250). They are mechanical abstractions of how native Solar magic works. A Solar using the Awareness Excellency isn't &quot;adding two dice to her pool&quot;, she's using magic to sharpen her senses to see things she couldn't otherwise see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1366559-inhuman-senses?p=1366576#post1366576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way this is worded implies that charms have to be in the same vein as Keen Sight Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1363139#post1363139\">You'd think, right?</a><br /> <br /> Note the wording on Flawlessly Impenatrable Disguise is &quot;Nor can it be thwarted by inhuman sensory acuity&quot;. Merely having inhuman senses is NOT enough to contest this Charm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-09-2020, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}